A Structured Approach to Practice
Rather than random problem-solving, consider this approach based on common advice from successful candidates:

Foundation Phase (Weeks 1–2)
Start with problems that teach fundamental operations:

Array manipulation (Two Sum, Best Time to Buy Stock)
String basics (Valid Palindrome, Valid Parentheses)
Linked list operations (Reverse Linked List, Merge Two Lists)
Tree basics (Inorder Traversal, Maximum Depth)
Pattern Recognition (Weeks 3–4)
Group problems by technique:

Sliding Window: Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters, Minimum Window Substring
Two Pointers: Container With Most Water, 3Sum
BFS/DFS: Number of Islands, Clone Graph
Basic DP: Climbing Stairs, House Robber
Integration Phase (Weeks 5–6)
Mix different problem types
Practice under time constraints
Focus on explaining your approach clearly
